  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SECURING HABITAT AND CONNECTIVITY TO SUSTAIN AMBOSELI&apos;S ELEPHANT POPULATION, INTEGRATING LAND LEASING, RANGERS OPERATIONS AND COMMUNITY STEWARDSHIP</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT AN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT ON COMMUNITY-OWNED LAND BETWEEN AMBOSELI AND CHYULU HILLS NATIONAL PARKS, KENYA, BY STRENGTHENING ELEPHANT PROTECTION, SECURING HABITAT CONNECTIVITY, AND ENHANCING HUMAN-ELEPHANT COEXISTENCE. AS PART OF THE KENYA RIFT VALLEY SAVANNA ELEPHANT STRONGHOLD, THIS ECOSYSTEM IS HOME TO APPROXIMATELY 12,814 ELEPHANTS. THIS PROJECT IS INTENDED TO CONSERVE AFRICAN SAVANNA ELEPHANTS AND THEIR HABITAT BY ADDRESSING THE IMPACTS OF POACHING, HABITAT LOSS, AND HUMAN-ELEPHANT CONFLICT (HEC). SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) IMPLEMENTING VOLUNTARY CONSERVATION LAND LEASE PROGRAMS THAT REDUCE HABITAT FRAGMENTATION AND PROVIDE BENEFIT SHARING AND LIVESTOCK GRAZING ACCESS FOR LANDOWNERS (2) EQUIPPING AND DEPLOYING COMMUNITY RANGER PATROLS (E.G., FUEL AND RATIONS) FOR MONITORING LAND-USE REGULATION COMPLIANCE AND CONDUCTING ANTI-POACHING AND HEC MITIGATION EFFORTS (3) DEVELOPING AND FACILITATING CONSERVANCY GOVERNANCE AND MANAGEMENT MECHANISMS FOR MARITE AND NAIRRABALA CONSERVANCIES (4) CREATING AND DEPLOYING A MULTI-AGENCY HABITAT PROTECTION UNIT, COMPRISED OF THE NATIONAL ENVIRONMENT MANAGEMENT AUTHORITY (NEMA), KAJIADO COUNTY GOVERNMENT (KCG), AND KENYA WILDLIFE SERVICE (KWS) (5) DEVELOPING A FENCING PLAN TO MITIGATE HEC ON THE NORTHERN BOUNDARY OF THE</narrative>
  </description>
